WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.771
Where the suite lives: tools.

2
00:00:02.051 --> 00:00:03.800
You don’t need a framework to start.

3
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:10.075
pytest is enough for many teams: one parametrized test per case (the docs show @pytest.

4
00:00:10.355 --> 00:00:11.101
mark.

5
00:00:11.381 --> 00:00:26.187
parametrize for running one test function over many inputs), deterministic assertions inline, a custom marker such as this course’s live marker for tests that call a model, and a small script that computes paired statistics from a results file.

6
00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:33.485
Its advantage is that the eval suite runs with the rest of your tests, in the same CI, with tools everyone knows.

7
00:00:33.765 --> 00:00:36.027
The labs in this program are built that way.

8
00:00:36.307 --> 00:00:43.944
Promptfoo is an open-source (MIT) command-line tool and library for evaluating and red-teaming LLM apps.

9
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:47.424
Cases live in a YAML config ( promptfooconfig.

10
00:00:47.704 --> 00:01:03.939
yaml in its examples) with assertions per test: deterministic ones such as equals, contains, is-json, regex, and custom python or javascript checks, model-graded ones such as llm-rubric and factuality, plus cost and latency.

11
00:01:04.219 --> 00:01:11.792
Its GitHub Action runs a before-and-after comparison when a pull request edits a prompt and posts a link to the results.

12
00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:21.971
Inspect is an open-source (MIT) framework for LLM evaluations developed by the UK AI Security Institute with Meridian Labs.

13
00:01:22.251 --> 00:01:32.021
An eval is a task that combines a dataset of samples, a solver that produces answers (from a single generate() call to a full agent), and a scorer.

14
00:01:32.301 --> 00:01:39.683
You run tasks with inspect eval, browse logs with inspect view, and it ships a large set of prebuilt evaluations.

15
00:01:39.963 --> 00:01:45.723
It suits agentic and multi-step evals, and teams who want detailed logs of every sample.

16
00:01:46.003 --> 00:01:52.104
OpenAI Evals is an open-source framework and registry of benchmarks from OpenAI.

17
00:01:52.384 --> 00:02:09.515
OpenAI also built a hosted Evals product on its platform, and its docs now say that the hosted Evals platform became read-only for existing users on October 31, 2026 and is scheduled to shut down on November 30, 2026.

18
00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:22.168
That’s a lesson in itself: keep your cases, graders, and results in your own repository in a portable format (JSONL plus code), so a vendor’s product decision can’t take your regression suite with it.

19
00:02:22.448 --> 00:02:26.587
How to choose: start with pytest unless a tool gives you something you need.

20
00:02:26.867 --> 00:02:32.861
Promptfoo is quick for prompt-level comparisons across several providers with a PR workflow.

21
00:02:33.141 --> 00:02:36.491
Inspect fits agent evals and research-grade logging.

22
00:02:36.771 --> 00:02:46.221
Whatever you pick, the statistics in lesson 7 and the decision rules above are yours to apply; none of these tools makes a noisy score significant.
